    {
      "id": "claim_329118edafcb4d068da0ab3475109959",
      "statement": "Middleware can implement either synchronous or asynchronous versions of lifecycle and interception hooks. The agent automatically detects the execution context (sync vs async) and invokes the appropriate version. If only one variant is implemented and the execution context requires the other, calling that hook raises NotImplementedError with guidance on how to resolve the mismatch.",
